content.text:
That's a **Supabase RLS warning** — it means Row Level Security is off on your tables. It's flagging it as a security notice.

For MVP this is fine — your data is read-only public info (farmer profiles, produce listings). No user accounts, no private data.

---

## To remove the warning (optional but good practice)

Run this in SQL Editor:

```sql
alter table farmers enable row level security;
alter table produce_listings enable row level security;
alter table reviews enable row level security;
alter table notify_requests enable row level security;
alter table media enable row level security;
alter table regions enable row level security;

-- Allow anyone to read public data
create policy "Public read farmers" on farmers for select using (true);
create policy "Public read produce" on produce_listings for select using (true);
create policy "Public read reviews" on reviews for select using (approved = true);
create policy "Public read media" on media for select using (true);
create policy "Public read regions" on regions for select using (true);

-- Allow anyone to insert notify requests
create policy "Public insert notify" on notify_requests for insert with check (true);
```

Run this → warning goes away → data is still publicly readable.

---

Tell me when done and we move to **setting up the Next.js project**.

